08:07:25 said  I rebuilt your own Proxzy-style network inspector as a desktop app: a traffic list and request inspector, copy URL/cURL/share, repeat, a Composer for GraphQL and REST, Map Local mock replies, Breakpoints you can edit and continue or abort, and a Log Dashboard. Everything is unlocked — there is no account, trial or paywall. The in-app **Guide & Stack** page teaches each feature in five steps and explains that it is built with Rust and egui/eframe, with real sends through the system's curl and local rules for mocks.
08:07:25 said  The build and the automatic picture check both pass. The honest difference from Proxyman is that this version does not yet intercept other apps' live HTTPS traffic or install a certificate; it starts from a demo traffic feed, so the original's exact look and wording are still estimates. The next thing I would add is a real local proxy engine so your own browser or app traffic appears automatically — and a screenshot or two of the original would let me fine-tune the layout.
