04:46:24 said  Implemented the ACP concept feature and tutorial update.
04:46:24 said  **What changed**
04:46:24 said  - Added **ACP Bridge** under *Automation & agents*, with a clear editor -> agent -> MCP tools -> Proxzy flow.
04:46:24 said  - Built an interactive 11-message ACP v1 session lab (`initialize`, `session/new`, `session/prompt`, updates, permission request, `stopReason`).
04:46:24 said  - Added a working permission gate with **Allow once**, **Always allow**, and **Reject**, including the correct stopped/refused outcome.
04:46:24 said  - Added copy-ready **Editor config**, **MCP entry**, and **Agent prompt** templates.
04:46:24 said  - Linked ACP Bridge from **Agent Control** and **Screen Play & MCP**.
04:46:24 said  - Updated the tutorial to a **13-stop tour** with a dedicated ACP stop and matching illustration.
04:46:24 said  - Documented the concept, demo triggers, and real-vs-simulated boundary.
04:46:24 said  **Verification**
04:46:24 said  - `cargo test`: **75 passed, 0 failed**
04:46:24 said  - Build: clean, no warnings
04:46:24 said  - Screenshots captured for the ACP page (pending, allowed, rejected), tutorial, tour, Agent Control, and Screen Play
04:46:24 said  - `rebuild_check`: **would pass**
04:46:26 said  The ACP Bridge now sits beside Agent Control so you can see the other half of the agent story: how an editor starts and supervises an AI agent in the first place. It walks through a realistic session, pauses before a side effect, and lets you approve or reject it. The screen is a learning simulation rather than a live connection, and it clearly separates ACP from MCP so the two are not confused. The tutorial now includes this stop, so the guided tour covers the full setup from editor to tools.
